Operating Systems Project #1
-----------------------------
Author: Lucas Lovellette
Date: 02/08/2025

Description:
------------
This project creates a simple multi-process system consisting of a parent process (oss) and a child process (user).
The oss process parses command line options to determine:
  - The total number of user processes to launch (-n)
  - The maximum number of simultaneous processes (-s)
  - The number of iterations for the user process (-t)

Each user process, when executed, prints its PID, its parent's PID, and the iteration count before and after a one-second sleep.

Files:
------
- oss.c      : Source code for the parent process (oss)
- user.c     : Source code for the child process (user)
- Makefile   : Build script that compiles both executables and provides a clean target
- README     : This file

Compilation:
------------
To compile the project, run:
    make
This will create the executables: oss and user.

Usage:
------
The parent process (oss) is invoked with the following options:
    -h         : Show help message and exit
    -n proc    : Total number of user processes to launch (default: 5)
    -s simul   : Maximum number of simultaneous user processes (default: 3)
    -t iter    : Number of iterations to pass to the user process (default: 7)

Example:
    To launch oss to create 5 user processes, with no more than 3 running concurrently and 7 iterations each:

    ./oss -n 5 -s 3 -t 7

Note:
-----
The user executable is intended to be launched by oss. However, you can test it individually by running:
    ./user 5

Version Control:
----------------
This project uses git for version control. Commit logs show daily progress and modifications.

Known Issues:
-------------
No major issues at this time.

Author Notes:
-------------
Before final submission, please run "make clean" to remove object files and executables.
